[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one parser bug, one fix queued. Its reports hold
three problems. The parser fix covers the biggest one only. The other two keep coming after it ships.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is not one issue. Each problem below has its own ticket and its own fix.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<SplitTable
  ticket={4471}
  tickets={{
    parser: 'https://github.com/codingpains/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1',
    hint: 'https://github.com/codingpains/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2',
    'one-day': 'https://github.com/codingpains/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3',
  }}
/>

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first. Every tenant on file writes the
  day first, so day and month swap. This is the bug #4471 describes, and the fix it has queued.
- **`hint`**: the `booking-v3` form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, people type the
  month first, and the form reads the date day first. Only bookings typed into that form, at the
  tenants who run it. The parser fix does not reach the form.
- **`one-day`**: the date moves by one day; day and month do not swap. The desk already read
  these as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`), but the #4471 page files them under the parser and
  only footnotes them. A meeting in Lisbon and Toronto landing on different days points at time
  zones. Not confirmed yet.

## How it was counted

- One id, one report. The export repeats some reports because its pages overlap; they count once.
- A report goes where its **tenant** puts it: the locale they write dates in and the booking form
  they run (`causes.ts`). The intake tag is a guess from the reporter's browser. It is shown in the
  table and used for nothing: it disagrees with the tenant in both directions.
- The desk's one-day reports count apart, under their own ticket.
- The table is built from the export at render time. If the queue grows, the numbers follow.

## What to do with #4471

- Keep #4471 for the parser. Do not close it as fixed for the other two.
- Matching on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) put all three
  in one ticket: the subjects match, the causes do not. Before merging during an incident, check
  that the tenant and the way the report came in point to the same cause.

